{
  "slug": "black-bean-stuffed-peppers",
  "name": "Black bean stuffed peppers",
  "description": "Bell pepper halves baked with a lightly spiced filling of black beans, brown rice, and zucchini.",
  "iconKey": "dome",
  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 400°F and halve the bell peppers lengthwise, hollowing out each half.",
    "Warm the olive oil in a skillet over medium heat, then soften the chopped onion and diced zucchini for about 3 minutes.",
    "Stir in the black beans, cooked brown rice, diced tomato, ground cumin, and chili powder, and cook 2 minutes more to draw out the aroma.",
    "Spoon the filling into the bell pepper halves and arrange them snugly in a baking dish.",
    "Bake for 25 minutes, until the bell peppers are tender and the filling is heated through."
